{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread","id":188087,"title":"Hunter: Cults, development revival thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-04T11:08:16-07:00","id":188087,"title":"Hunter: Cults, development revival thread","content":"So for a while I have found myself without a project, and quite a few people have expressed interest in <a href=\"http://hunter-the-vigil-cults.wikia.com/wiki/Hunter_the_Vigil:_Cults_Wiki\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter: Cults</a>. So lets give a try,<br /> <br /> <br /> For those of you who don't already know, the goals of Cults are as follows:<ul><li>To present a dark mirror of Compacts and Conspiracies, just as Slasher presetned a dark mirror of individual Hunters.</li> <li>To explore the way heroic Hunter Compacts and Conspiracies slide down the slope towards cultdom - with a theme of isolation.</li> <li>To present Compacts and Conspiracies as actual organisations.</li> </ul><br /> Along with the following lesser goals:<ul><li>To explore the vigil's isolating effects. A Compact where everyone maintains strong ties to mundane life is pretty safe. A Compact where members only really talk to each-other is in the danger zone.</li> <li>To embrace the mostly overlooked theme of faith and religion in Hunter. There's a lot of Compacts and Conspiracies that are explicitly religious and a few more that are spiritual. But after all this time, there's not much for storytellers who want to have a Christian angel visit their Long Night players or the Biblical Lucifer contact his child in the Lcuifuge.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> So if you're interested catch up on the wiki and start posting ideas. Just to get started, I feel that the third goal - To present Compacts and Conspiracies as actual organisations - has been neglected and have just started thinking about creating Endowments that play to the ideas of large organisation. Either an Endowment that's explicitly used to organisation or an Endowment that basically requires 15 or more Hunters in the current scene. Though due to a coincidence, the Ascending Ones already have one (they need an Endowment that's slightly cult like instead)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T21:15:46-07:00","id":188479,"title":"","content":"I think that cults are problematic territory and a 'dark mirror' approach would perhaps rob them of even more humanity and push it further into shallow victimhood. The hero/cultist dichotomy you mention does little to assuage my concerns, I'm afraid. Have you considered these pitfalls?<br /> <br /> ps Have you seen the movie 'The Master' starring Philip Seymour Hoffman in your research? I haven't and would like to know if it's worth a viewing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:31:37-07:00","id":233251,"title":"","content":"From what I read, an interesting issue to consider is whether the supernatural, ironically, would cause people to question their faith. <br /> <br /> To explain, Vampires, for example, are clearly unaffected by traditional holy objects, and aren't consistently either. Additionally, for all the monsters running around... where are the Angels? From the Hunter's POV, they are nowhere to be seen. This, and other examples of how the monsters essentially refuse to respond to what is supposed to hurt them under religious gospel, traditionally from what I know anyway, I'd think would raise questions.<br /> <br /> Now, the Long Night does have an interesting response to this question, but how could this impact others view of their faith? After all, shouldn't say, the Abrahamic God, from a religious perspective, intervene most when there are supernatural entities running around? And for those who do find out about the God Machine... well, again, I doubt in most cases it'd match their perception of what they think the Abrahamic God should be, for example. <br /> <br /> <br /> I did actually see Cults have an interesting response to this, with the whole cult that summons demons to protect its followers, however I'd think it could use more exploration, if religion is a major theme. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T14:51:02-07:00","id":233286,"title":"","content":"Well there are angels running around. Even if you don't count the God Machine, there's still the Principle and the Empyerian (which sadly only got one single sidebar).<br /> <br /> However I would argue that for the most part, the things you raise are just another variant of theodicies (aka, why didn't god stop Hitler?). I'm pretty sure the bible doesn't actually &quot;and ye, a crucifix shall frighten the undead&quot;, I'm not sure if folk-tales or Hollywood made it up. But I think from a purely rational perspective, a vampire shouldn't be any bigger challenge to a Christian's faith than Hitler.<br /> <br /> <br /> But then, when was religion ever &quot;purely rational&quot;?<br /> <br /> There's a bit of stuff here and there. The Malleus' write up explicitly talks about why they don't use Benedictions to convert people. The Athenic Church is popular precisely because it's Goddess is more visibly active in defending Her people. Maybe God is constantly helping the Malleus and/or the Long Night, but he's way more subtle about it, Minerva actually says to heir priestesses &quot;yo, a vampire has her eye on Julia, take this lightning bolt and fry her&quot;. Prometheus' Fire in chapter five talks about having faith in an invisible god while you're fighting a visible one.<br /> <br /> <br /> But you are right. There is room for more on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:08:33-07:00","id":233321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=233286#post233286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well there are angels running around. Even if you don't count the God Machine, there's still the Principle and the Empyerian (which sadly only got one single sidebar).</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgot about those, although... are either very developed or even remotely common? Additionally, do they act like biblical Angels? <br /> <br /> The last part is important because, essentially, I'd argue religion would create an expectation for how the supernatural should act. Breaking those expectations, to me, would hurt people's faith, because they aren't acting according to how the local preacher said they should. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However I would argue that for the most part, the things you raise are just another variant of theodicies (aka, why didn't god stop Hitler?). I'm pretty sure the bible doesn't actually &quot;and ye, a crucifix shall frighten the undead&quot;, I'm not sure if folk-tales or Hollywood made it up. But I think from a purely rational perspective, a vampire shouldn't be any bigger challenge to a Christian's faith than Hitler. </div> </div> </div>I think a reason this would be different is that, shouldn't the purely supernatural be more explicitly God's domain? I mean, from what I know, a lot of religion is essentially based around protecting yourself from the wrath of a supernatural deity in a way, so, in a way, shouldn't it protect you from say, Vampires or Werewolves? For that matter, didn't real world religion frequently gain power from promising to protect from say, Demons?<br /> <br /> Additionally, Folk-Tales are incredibly important to religion, to put things mildly, so even if say, the Bible doesn't explicitly say Vampires should be hurt by crucifix, shouldn't that all the folk-tales, and later on yes Hollywood, saying that they do, and then them not, have some sort of impact? It'd be saying, in the case of the former in some cases, that religious authorities are outright wrong. <br /> <br /> By contrast, Hitler is a much more human affair, if you will. I mean, yes, the argument still applies, but it isn't quite as strong, because religion didn't explicitly promise as much to protect you from human murderers. Demons, and other supernatural threats though? I'd think that be a bit more explicit of a promise. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But then, when was religion ever &quot;purely rational&quot;?<br /> <br /> There's a bit of stuff here and there. The Malleus' write up explicitly talks about why they don't use Benedictions to convert people. The Athenic Church is popular precisely because it's Goddess is more visibly active in defending Her people. Maybe God is constantly helping the Malleus and/or the Long Night, but he's way more subtle about it, Minerva actually says to heir priestesses &quot;yo, a vampire has her eye on Julia, take this lightning bolt and fry her&quot;. Prometheus' Fire in chapter five talks about having faith in an invisible god while you're fighting a visible one. </div> </div> </div>Don't the Benedictions themselves even have elements that actually would cause people to question their nature? For example, that when they're used to revive people to life, they are apparently horrified by what they saw, and this, I think, was with people that should've seen Heaven or similar.<br /> <br /> Its also worth noting that I'd imagine Hunter faith would be shaken, a lot, by finding out how easily certain monsters can pretend to be Demons. I mean, are Demons supposed to be able to look like Angels, and have no ability to tell the difference? That'd be scary, I'd imagine, for the average Christian I'd imagine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But you are right. There is room for more on this. </div> </div> </div>Other thoughts I have here is Null Mysteris essentially arguing that, &quot;yeah, you may have benedictions, but you hardly are the only one with miracles. How do you explain all the others?&quot; Essentially, if the supernatural is everywhere, no one can prove their God is true, if you will, because miracles are hardly relegated to them. I mean, how would a Muslim or even say, a Protestant Christian, respond to seeing a Benediction? Or for that matter, the tricks available to explicitly unreligious Conspiracies, that are magical, yet not religious at all, such as those of the Cheiron Group? They could perhaps blame Demons, but that only gets one so far, because again, why would God leave his followers defenseless while letting the heretics and unbelievers have all the power? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:56:52-07:00","id":233365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=233321#post233321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgot about those, although... are either very developed or even remotely common? Additionally, do they act like biblical Angels?</div> </div> </div> </div> The Principle is developed, no mention on how common it's angels are. The Emperian was barely developed at all.<br /> <br /> The Principle sort of act like biblical angels; including the plague spreading type to visit Egypt in exodus. The Emperian... are barely developed at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=233321#post233321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a reason this would be different is that, shouldn't the purely supernatural be more explicitly God's domain?</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think so. I don't believe the Abrahamic religions say so; they do say something like that for Infernal demons, which is reflected in the mechanics for Inferno.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=233321#post233321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, Folk-Tales are incredibly important to religion, to put things mildly, so even if say, the Bible doesn't explicitly say Vampires should be hurt by crucifix, shouldn't that all the folk-tales, and later on yes Hollywood, saying that they do, and then them not, have some sort of impact?</div> </div> </div> </div> The real question is why did folk-tales ever start saying vampires should be hurt by crucifix?<br /> <br /> In the WoD people know about the supernatural, they just don't talk about it. I think you could explain the crucifix as part of the lie - everyone knows they don't hurt vampires, just like everyone knows vampires exist. But in both cases they pretend, becuase it's comforting.<br /> <br /> In that case I don't think it will affect the faith of many; their faith is protected by the same self-deception. Only hunters will ever face that crisis of faith, and I'm sure both the Long Night and the MM have well rehursed explenations; probably starting with &quot;the bible never said that&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=233321#post233321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't the Benedictions themselves even have elements that actually would cause people to question their nature? For example, that when they're used to revive people to life, they are apparently horrified by what they saw, and this, I think, was with people that should've seen Heaven or similar.</div> </div> </div> </div> They do. But they're in a grey area, there's stuff that can suggest they're not quite godly but there's also stuff that suggests they might be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=233321#post233321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, are Demons supposed to be able to look like Angels, and have no ability to tell the difference? That'd be scary, I'd imagine, for the average Christian I'd imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div> Probably; I mean, biblical angels look pretty terrifying and Satan is The Father of Lies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=233321#post233321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other thoughts I have here is Null Mysteris essentially arguing that, &quot;yeah, you may have benedictions, but you hardly are the only one with miracles. How do you explain all the others?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> That's exactly how the NM write up goes; but with more of a moral slant to it. <br /> <br /> Well you can bring back the dead using catholic prayer, that's evidence god exists. Now where's your evidence for him being stronger than Zeus and where's your evidence for his moral authority?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T16:12:13-07:00","id":233374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=233365#post233365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Principle is developed, no mention on how common it's angels are. The Emperian was barely developed at all.<br /> <br /> The Principle sort of act like biblical angels; including the plague spreading type to visit Egypt in exodus. The Emperian... are barely developed at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, to say the least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think so. I don't believe the Abrahamic religions say so; they do say something like that for Infernal demons, which is reflected in the mechanics for Inferno. </div> </div> </div>Didn't the Catholic Church during the Middle Ages, for example, constantly promise to protect people from supernatural threats that had roots in things like folklore? <br /> <br /> My point here is that while the Bible may not explicitly say such, a lot of Christian institutions have in the past(to be fair, not in the present to my knowledge.) And disrupting what Christian institutions, for example, say is the case screws with this, even if the Bible doesn't promise such. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The real question is why did folk-tales ever start saying vampires should be hurt by crucifix? </div> </div> </div>Again, I think during the Middle Ages, not sure though. <br /> <br /> My point with this is that, again, I'd argue religious institutions, and later on, other parts of culture have built up expectations for how the supernatural would act if they existed. Having those assumptions broken would, I'd argue, cause problems with one's faith. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the WoD people know about the supernatural, they just don't talk about it. I think you could explain the crucifix as part of the lie - everyone knows they don't hurt vampires, just like everyone knows vampires exist. But in both cases they pretend, becuase it's comforting. </div> </div> </div>I see your point, but my problem is I don't completely agree with this interpretation per say. <br /> <br /> To explain, WOD to me is that the elites know of the supernatural, and that most everyday people have something that clouds said view, such as recent ideas introduced in Mage, and the God Machine I'm sure scheming to hide it. Now, they be sort of aware, but how much? I doubt they'd know that crucifixes won't hurt Vampires, for example. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In that case I don't think it will affect the faith of many; their faith is protected by the same self-deception. Only hunters will ever face that crisis of faith, and I'm sure both the Long Night and the MM have well rehursed explenations; probably starting with &quot;the bible never said that&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Ah, but that's where a problem would come up. Now, the Long Night has a reason why God isn't intervening more, humanity essentially has to prove itself. What does MM have, other than benedictions which are shaky evidence as noted?<br /> <br /> Additionally, an odd curve ball here are monsters that are explicitly Christian, such as the huge group of Vampires that are apparently Orthodox Christians. Shouldn't that cause some awkwardness for these groups? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Probably; I mean, biblical angels look pretty terrifying and Satan is The Father of Lies. </div> </div> </div>See, this is where modern perception matters. Now, yes, originally, biblical angels were terrifying, to put things mildly. However, how many modern Christians actually know that? Would they appreciate a God that had Angels that look far more like what Demons are supposed to? <br /> <br /> Now, the point with Satan is good, however would that hold up if they say, became aware of the God Machine? Just using an example. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's exactly how the NM write up goes; but with more of a moral slant to it.<br /> <br /> Well you can bring back the dead using catholic prayer, that's evidence god exists. Now where's your evidence for him being stronger than Zeus and where's your evidence for his moral authority? </div> </div> </div>True. But yeah, essentially, a world with multiple Gods, all of whom seem to have equal power, hurts traditional religious institutions I'd argue, because... they're essentially competition that can demonstrate their deity better. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also? There's something that acts as an awkward elephant in the room for both MM, the Long Night, and, I'm guessing, pretty much any other Abrahamic religious hunter group. From my understanding, humans are always supposed to have free will under the biblical view. What does one do when they meet monsters that can explicitly destroy that free will, and have done so repeatedly, including to fellow hunters? Doesn't it hurt the Abrahamic worldview if human free will can be so easily taken away? <br /> <br /> All of these are just thoughts I've had from how the supernatural, ironically, would heavily disrupt religious faith, rather than enforce it, which I think would be an interesting angle to pursue with Cults.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T11:49:08-07:00","id":234457,"title":"","content":"Um, Killer300? You're demonstrably wrong on two points:<br /> <br /> One, the vampiric Masquerade in Blood and Smoke is called out as not actually caring if the common man knows vampires exist or not, only their actual abilities, weaknesses, and who is actually a vampire. The elites have nothing to do with it, though they know too.<br /> <br /> Second, beliefs tend to not break when tested by outside sources, it becomes more ironclad if it's actually that important to their self-image. Scientific fact.<br /> <br /> As for the project, I actually made a good example of a Tier Three cult looking to become a Tier Four at some point if they learn to communicate with their gods reliably without going insane (themselves) as part of my stillborn Scarred Lands/nWoD crossover. I could dredge them up for you if you're open to nihilistic Buddhist mastermind psychics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T11:53:06-07:00","id":234465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=233374#post233374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't the Catholic Church during the Middle Ages, for example, constantly promise to protect people from supernatural threats that had roots in things like folklore?</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe?<br /> <br /> I haven't seen Flyboy in a while, and I usaully rely on him for info. Mind you, in the WoD the MM actually did that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=233374#post233374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see your point, but my problem is I don't completely agree with this interpretation per say.<br /> <br /> To explain, WOD to me is that the elites know of the supernatural, and that most everyday people have something that clouds said view, such as recent ideas introduced in Mage, and the God Machine I'm sure scheming to hide it. Now, they be sort of aware, but how much? I doubt they'd know that crucifixes won't hurt Vampires, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sleeping Curse is explicitly less effective against non-Supernal magic. So I think mortals have to know. Maybe not in detail but they'd know that the supernatural isn't safe or easily thwarted with religion, beucase if they didn't think that - they wouldn't be so scared that they supress the knowledge.<br /> <br /> Besides. Look at the question in the God Machine Chronicles. It's &quot;what have you forgotten&quot;. Anyone who discovers first hand that the vampire isn't affected by a crucifix would most probably forget it afterwords.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=233374#post233374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does MM have, other than benedictions which are shaky evidence as noted?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm sure they have something, in the real world the Catholic Church is very very good at justifying God's lack of direct intervention.<br /> <br /> Plus, I think that on the surface Benedictions are very strong evidence; it's only when you look a lot deeper that you start to find things that might cause questions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=233374#post233374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, an odd curve ball here are monsters that are explicitly Christian, such as the huge group of Vampires that are apparently Orthodox Christians. Shouldn't that cause some awkwardness for these groups?</div> </div> </div> </div> Nah, that's not an issue. To the MM they're like the Westbro Baptist Church (or Prosistants if you're very hard line). They call themselves christian, but they're not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=233374#post233374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, this is where modern perception matters. Now, yes, originally, biblical angels were terrifying, to put things mildly. However, how many modern Christians actually know that? Would they appreciate a God that had Angels that look far more like what Demons are supposed to?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think that if they saw and were terrified of an angel, the bible and the priests all pointing out that this is perfectly normal could help them get over the initial shock.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=233374#post233374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the point with Satan is good, however would that hold up if they say, became aware of the God Machine? Just using an example.</div> </div> </div> </div> If they truely have faith, they might call the G-M stronger than a vampire but weaker than God.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=233374#post233374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. But yeah, essentially, a world with multiple Gods, all of whom seem to have equal power, hurts traditional religious institutions I'd argue, because... they're essentially competition that can demonstrate their deity better.</div> </div> </div> </div> An adult is stronger than a child, but an ant can't tell the difference. I'm sure any priest can make a similar argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=233374#post233374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also? There's something that acts as an awkward elephant in the room for both MM, the Long Night, and, I'm guessing, pretty much any other Abrahamic religious hunter group. From my understanding, humans are always supposed to have free will under the biblical view. What does one do when they meet monsters that can explicitly destroy that free will, and have done so repeatedly, including to fellow hunters? Doesn't it hurt the Abrahamic worldview if human free will can be so easily taken away?</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't think so. I know the Catholic church does believe in demonic possession (Legion from the bible had it pretty bad).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think that ultimately in the WoD there are two types of people.<br /> <br /> The first type is ordinary people, who would outright dismiss any evidence of the supernatural, and that includes all the evidence that contradicts religion.<br /> The second type are hunters; who're the sort to look deeper. A religious hunter is certainly going to be shaken when they first see evidence that challanges their beleif, but they're hunters. When challanged they'll fight back. Some will discover doctrines similar to the Long Night, some will turn their backs on faith, and some will look for more protective gods. Sometimes they'll find someone like the Athenic Church, other times it's more like the Sheltering Spire.<br /> <br /> But since most people aren't hunters - I don't think the catholic church is in trouble any time soon. There's a lot of great stories when a Hunter's faith is challanged, but it's only the hunter's who face that story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T11:53:44-07:00","id":234466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=234457#post234457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the project, I actually made a good example of a Tier Three cult looking to become a Tier Four at some point if they learn to communicate with their gods reliably without going insane (themselves) as part of my stillborn Scarred Lands/nWoD crossover. I could dredge them up for you if you're open to nihilistic Buddhist mastermind psychics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am <b>always</b> interested in nihilistic Buddhist mastermind psychics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T12:01:46-07:00","id":234494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=234457#post234457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, Killer300? You're demonstrably wrong on two points:</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, that's fine, I admit to not having full knowledge of the NWOD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One, the vampiric Masquerade in Blood and Smoke is called out as not actually caring if the common man knows vampires exist or not, only their actual abilities, weaknesses, and who is actually a vampire. The elites have nothing to do with it, though they know too. </div> </div> </div>Well, not all do, however a few probably do, such as really high ranking government officials(yes, I admit even this is hazy.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, beliefs tend to not break when tested by outside sources, it becomes more ironclad if it's actually that important to their self-image. Scientific fact. </div> </div> </div>With normal disruptions, such as say external invasion. Supernatural disruptions screw everything over here, as no, I don't buy the religious are going to react exactly the same way to the supernatural intentionally ignoring their religious beliefs as say, the scientific community, or the state trying to stamp them out(yes, obviously, the last two are different extremes, but they illustrate something.)<br /> <br /> As again, doesn't religion promise to protect from supernatural threats?<br /> <br /> So no, this isn't demonstrable, and it isn't a scientific fact. because all your examples would be using non-supernatural threats, and wouldn't have miracles that are clearly NOT of the parent religion.<br /> <br /> There's also some historical counters, but that's territory for another time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the project, I actually made a good example of a Tier Three cult looking to become a Tier Four at some point if they learn to communicate with their gods reliably without going insane (themselves) as part of my stillborn Scarred Lands/nWoD crossover. I could dredge them up for you if you're open to nihilistic Buddhist mastermind psychics. </div> </div> </div>Ooh! This sounds interesting although... bizarre.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","user":"Killer300","date":". 08-19-2014, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T12:19:43-07:00","id":234528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=234465#post234465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Maybe?<br /> <br /> I haven't seen Flyboy in a while, and I usaully rely on him for info. Mind you, in the WoD the MM actually did that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Sleeping Curse is explicitly less effective against non-Supernal magic. So I think mortals have to know. Maybe not in detail but they'd know that the supernatural isn't safe or easily thwarted with religion, beucase if they didn't think that - they wouldn't be so scared that they supress the knowledge.<br /> <br /> Besides. Look at the question in the God Machine Chronicles. It's &quot;what have you forgotten&quot;. Anyone who discovers first hand that the vampire isn't affected by a crucifix would most probably forget it afterwords. </div> </div> </div>True, and my point elsewhere with elites was put, rightly, into question.<br /> <br /> However, even so, its worth noting VALKYRIE, and the Cheiron Group still have a lot of misconceptions when fighting monsters, suggesting some things there. Now, yes, they aren't quite the religious groups we're discussing, but they're an interesting example of human biases related to the supernatural persisting, and possibly being re-shocked by them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm sure they have something, in the real world the Catholic Church is very very good at justifying God's lack of direct intervention.<br /> <br /> Plus, I think that on the surface Benedictions are very strong evidence; it's only when you look a lot deeper that you start to find things that might cause questions. </div> </div> </div>Sure, I'm just trying to figure out what those may be. Keep in mind, I'm more doing this to ask questions which I just think maybe should be answered in the supplement, as religion is a major theme within it. Questions of faith to me should be one of those.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nah, that's not an issue. To the MM they're like the Westbro Baptist Church (or Prosistants if you're very hard line). They call themselves christian, but they're not. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, I'd think it'd depend on the Hunter. Also, they're also useful as it may give a religious person a reason to believe that not all monsters are evil, or even unholy necessarily, seeing as they can share belief in God and all.<br /> <br /> I bring that up because opportunities for Hunters to work with monsters( obviously, not MM's deal), are something I love to encourage the possibility of, and this is one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that if they saw and were terrified of an angel, the bible and the priests all pointing out that this is perfectly normal could help them get over the initial shock. </div> </div> </div>True, although if the Angels then go on to do some brutal<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they truely have faith, they might call the G-M stronger than a vampire but weaker than God. </div> </div> </div>Doesn't its existence kind of validate the Gnostic point of view? Like, a lot? Because having a higher God begs awkward issues.<br /> <br /> Now, to be fair, this is mostly a moot issue, as I don't think even a fair amount of the Conspiracies know what the God Machine is, much less the average Hunter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An adult is stronger than a child, but an ant can't tell the difference. I'm sure any priest can make a similar argument. </div> </div> </div>Ooh! Interesting argument, to say the least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think so. I know the Catholic church does believe in demonic possession (Legion from the bible had it pretty bad). </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but still, isn't a major part of Christianity the belief in free will? Also, doesn't Demonic Possession<br /> <br /> I think that ultimately in the WoD there are two types of people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The first type is ordinary people, who would outright dismiss any evidence of the supernatural, and that includes all the evidence that contradicts religion.<br /> The second type are hunters; who're the sort to look deeper. A religious hunter is certainly going to be shaken when they first see evidence that challanges their beleif, but they're hunters. When challanged they'll fight back. Some will discover doctrines similar to the Long Night, some will turn their backs on faith, and some will look for more protective gods. Sometimes they'll find someone like the Athenic Church, other times it's more like the Sheltering Spire.<br /> <br /> But since most people aren't hunters - I don't think the catholic church is in trouble any time soon. There's a lot of great stories when a Hunter's faith is challanged, but it's only the hunter's who face that story. </div> </div> </div>Of course, I should've said upfront this is more a discussion for Hunters than normal mortals(although Stigmatics and the like are interesting here.)<br /> <br /> Hence, I just want to have a discussion of this type of thing to give possible plot hooks for players, and offer how perhaps the religious answer certain questions.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T15:19:53-07:00","id":234713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=234466#post234466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am <b>always</b> interested in nihilistic Buddhist mastermind psychics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, here's the into writeup. Keep in mind I also intended them to be the co-conspirators in chronicles where the slarecian race (psychic projections of godlike alien intellects that were trapped in the world as it formed, and absolutely <i>hate </i>it) are the main antagonists, so that's what I'm referring to when I say slarecian, uthriarch (the godlike alien intellects in question), or god-king, and they're based on Second Sight rules. The language virus is a nasty trick taught by their masters, it overwrites the normal lingual centers of the brain with the incomprehensible-to-humans slarecian language and makes the vectors only able to understand slarecian likewise. It only lasts for a month or so, but by that point the infected are institutionalized.<br /> <br /> <b>Cult: The Order of Divine Shade</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Religions that deny the flesh and irrational to exalt the spirit and rational are nothing new. Buddhism, one of the world's largest religions, is based on that idea at its core, and all the other major world religions, Islam, Christianity, Judaism, and Hinduism have elements of it. All agree that the flesh is a creature of weakness and vice, and an impediment to the virtuous spirit and soul.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Most devout adherents of said religions would find the idea of </span></span></span><i>destroying</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> that flesh to protect the spirit both horrifying and ridiculous-besides the whole &quot;survival instinct&quot; thing, you can't improve the spirit if you're dead, and suicide does nothing but hurt the world around you. Nonetheless, most is not all, and there are those who somehow think removing themselves from the world is helping it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Somewhere beyond that would be the slarecian cult priest, who thinks removing </span></span></span><i>everything</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> is somehow helping it. Cults are not known for their abilities in the &quot;logic&quot; department.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">True it's only the truly high-ranking members, the direct lieutenants of any reborn slarecians and the hands of the uthriachs that truly buy into the whole &quot;destroy the universe to save it&quot; line, and that's partially the influence of the God-Kings speaking. But still, they wouldn't have been as receptive to the Formless Ones' nihilistic view of things if they hadn't already hated the world-the one commonality between all slarecian cults.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Of course, one doesn't come to despise the world without the world doing something to you first, and most servants of the mind tyrants have had bitter experience with life. Most slarecian cultists have suffered greatly in the past, and most of those for one particular reason that draws them to the attention of the uthriach's vast intellects-psionics. By accident of birth, two-edged supernatural gift, or exposure to a mutant strain of the slarecian language virus, there is no shortage of humans in the World of Darkness with some degree of psychic ability. Most of this is small enough to be unnoticed, and deliberately so in order to make the world seem far, far saner than it is, but there is always going to be the outlier (especially in the last case, where temporary aphasia is the cause). Humans being humans, their first reaction is to shun what scares them and force the psychic in question to &quot;tell the truth&quot; about their abilities being clever hoaxes, or just force them into exile among the crowds, unable to connect to the people who run away.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Enter the cultists.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The first step is usually to befriend the alienated psychic in question. This is usually the easiest step, as it is a rare one who has been burned that badly by a false friend in any world, even one of Darkness, and the psychic is usually desperate for a sympathetic ear. From there, it's a little more work to convince the psychic that the problem lies with the rest of the world and the nature of flesh itself, and not them, but that's a pretty low bar to clear. Nor is convincing them to take a special concoction, brewed from the blood of slarecian shadowmen that puts them in brief but direct communion with the minds of the Formless Ones.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The hard part is convincing them that, once they have had the dream of the uthriachs, that the instinctual fear they have of such callous beings is simply that their minds are too attached to their bodies, and that was the mere uncanny valley effect applied to individuals who obviously no longer need their own bodies-something alien to the naive human experience. Often, it doesn't work, at which point the failed recruit is either murdered or hit with the Betrayal of Memory rite, whatever causes less of a mess. But sometimes, especially with those who have become disgusted with the human condition altogether, it does, and they see the raw power that could be theirs-the raw power to take what the world owes them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The truly nihilistic teachings come later, but by that point, the cultist is usually so immersed in mystery cult brainwashing and community that they simply nod their head along to the idea that the world must be returned to a place of pure thought and chaos, devoid of the pain of flesh.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And thanks to the ability of the God-Kings to telepathically network cultists through linking dreams, they are usually quite competently organized in carrying out that idea. And by far the largest and most organized is the hidden pseudo-Gnostic fraternity known as the Cult of Divine Shade.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Shades are an old organization. How old is obscured by a thick layer of obfuscation and false leads, not all of them intentional. From what little can be gleaned, the Order came into being around the same time that the Gnostic Christians were deemed heretics and hunted down to the last, in the 4th century AD. Said gleaning also implies they were largely responsible for the declaration of heresy by the early Catholics-and deliberately so, the Gnostics having seen their formation for the ill omen it was, although they did not realize how truly insane these &quot;abusers of enlightenment&quot; were.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">This implied manipulation speaks to the </span></span></span><i>modus operandi </i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">of the Shades-while the Catholics were already seeking to consolidate their power, and the Order quietly pressured them into consolidating said power at the expense of an enemy. Thus, their basic tactic-manipulate, pressure, and puppet, all to trick their enemies into destroying themselves, and giving ample chaos as a cover to work under.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And with the power to manipulate minds, the ability of the Shades to do that is great indeed.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">While not all members of the Order are psychics, enough are to the point where the Shades usually have more than enough mental trickery to accomplish whatever false flag scheme they plan and infiltration. And they are quite good at both, given how their desires for whatever institution they quietly commandeer-either they want a good vantage point to seek out recruits or they want the best place to turn others against their enemies from. Thus, they tend to take over things like psychology departments, insane asylums, or neighborhood watch organizations, usually by finding someone with a loud voice or high-up and then figuring out how to best mentally influence them into courses of actions suitable to their agenda. If they have their way, even their agents won't know that they're working for the Shades.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Beyond those two motivations, the basic goals of the cult are twofold-refine and hone their psychic strength, and resurrect the &quot;Sophic Children&quot;-the slarecians. The first is simple enough to understand, but is actually a little more altruistic than it seems-most of the Shades suffered greatly for their powers, and indeed that's why they came to the attention of recruiters. Their quest to understand the source and nature of their powers is at least partially so they can teach others to control theirs and avoid the pain they went through (as members of the Order, but still..). The second is both more pragmatic and more involved: The Shades take it as an item of reality that the assistance of a Prince of Mind, with their divine psionics and instinctive mastery over social matters make them ideal leaders, as well as galvanizing overall to have the patronage of a demigod behind a particular chapter. It's also hard as hell-besides requiring a specific, level-five version of the Compel the God rite (and there's only a few people even capable of that level of power, let alone have that one rite), and several powerful psychics (one focusing on a different discipline each), it also requires slarecian relics from deep under the earth, the correct calculations for the ritual drawing, and for it to be cast in during &quot;void of reason&quot;-which is to say, complete anarchy where there is no form of hierarchy at all in the immediate area, except for the Order, which is harder than it sounds; The rite takes a long while to prepare and cast, and anarchy is quickly undone as legitimate authorities reestablish their power or criminals fill the void. But that's breaking a hole, however small, in a prison for alien gods long enough for them to pod off a smaller version of themselves for you, and the benefits far outweigh any losses.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T15:48:54-07:00","id":234742,"title":"","content":"I'm going to be honest here; I think there's some good ideas - evil Buddhist psychics, bodyless god-psychic minds, but you're putting all the focus in the wrong place and you're diluting the concept with too much generic-evil-cult.<br /> <br /> <br /> First of all, you need some way to tie the core thematic elements together. You need some aspect of Buddhist philosophy that can tie into the nihilism. You should base their methods of indoctrination on how Buddhist monks are actually trained - <a href=\"http://www.newyorker.com/magazine/2013/06/24/last-call-3\" target=\"_blank\">read this (start about half way down) for example</a>. Again, the recruits should have a Buddhist themed reason for joining up, being shunned for having powers is a very western troupe, I don't know if it's shared with eastern media but it still feels western. The Slarecians also should be made more Buddhist; ideally you should discover if there's any equivalent in Buddhist mythology to selling your soul to the evil. Try and find what motivated those mythological Buddhists to do evil and work that into the Shade-Slarecians relationship. Also the prefix -ian is pretty western. <br /> <br /> Also, there's no need to mention Catholicism or have them be active west of Tibet; at least not before modern transport. They should stand on their own.<br /> <br /> <br /> In general though your priorities should be in order:<br /> <br /> 1) Reinforcing a strong central theme: Nihilistic Buddhist mastermind psychics.<br /> 2) Stuff that's helpful for a storyteller or player trying to portray an individual charachter.<br /> 3) Stuff that's useful for a storyteller trying to portray the organisation as a whole.<br /> <br /> <br /> I would suggest trying to make the write up short but sweet. At least for myself, I find it's easier to write a good short - corebook sized - Hunter organisation than a longer one like the Canites or Knights of St George. It's harder to keep a longer piece of text focused.<br /> <br /> <br /> @Killer300, I think we've exhausted the current line of conversation. All that's left is to think up specific ideas for including hunters having a crisis of faith than can go into the project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T16:19:07-07:00","id":234758,"title":"","content":"Okay. I actually just cross-posted it without changing it, at all, and now I realize I was inspired by Gnosticism more than anything.<br /> <br /> I knew I had to rewrite it, just wanted your opinion on the start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T17:12:41-07:00","id":234819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> @Killer300, I think we've exhausted the current line of conversation. All that's left is to think up specific ideas for including hunters having a crisis of faith than can go into the project. </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I'll maybe put a Compact together later that kind of reflects stuff on that, but otherwise, everything that needed to be said there has been. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T00:06:16-07:00","id":235141,"title":"","content":"@Leliel So thinking a bit more about the evil psychic buddhists, this is what I came up with. It should definitely be checked for authenticity.<br /> <br /> <br /> Their philosophy is an extreme form of Buddhist asceticism. You know how Buddha found his middle path, well Jesus said &quot;judge not&quot; (looking at you Westbro Baptist Church). They take asceticism to such an extreme that they let their bodies die - and they think of themselves as teachers with the goal of makeing everyone do the same for their own good.<br /> <br /> They use monk-like training to reach altered states of consciousness where the god-minds can communicate with them; the god-minds teach them psychic powers which lets them detach from their bodies and become beings of pure psychic energy. While in this state they must feed on other beings psychic energy - basically they need 1 Willpower point a day, and since they have no more Virtue or Vice (Nilhisim!) they eat Willpower points. At first they just feed of their own uninhabited body, but it still ages and eventually dies. At which point they're thematically similar to <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Preta\" target=\"_blank\">Preta</a>.<br /> <br /> So you essentially have disembodied psychic Buddhist monks controlling their old bodies like a Puppet while feeding of it. And just to top it off their bodies basically shut down without a mind or soul inside - only rudimentry brain activity is left, but that's enough to feed off - so they have to preserve them; but they still end up puppeting bodies that look like Sokushinbutsu for most of their life.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the god-minds themselves; who knows or cares what they actually are. The cult thinks of them as Bodhavistas - they could have attained enlightenment but they chose to remain and teach others. All we know is that they can train you to be psychic; and they're promoting this nhilistic idea that everyone should be freed from worldly desires by abandoning their bodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T07:22:32-07:00","id":235389,"title":"","content":"One idea I've been toying with is a survivalist group, on the surface anyway, that tries to makes it members monster-proof somehow. Inevitably, the only way to really do that is some sort of supernatural benefit, and would also imply they somehow can resist say, mind control on a level most can't. Where this becomes cult like, besides some very possibly negative effects from the supernatural part, is that this group becomes... well, isolated. That, and how the cult preys on similar people as to how a Cult will, as they're trying to transform as much of humanity as possible into something that would be immune, or at least highly resistant, to the mind altering abilities of the supernatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T11:44:13-07:00","id":235608,"title":"","content":"If I'm honest, that sounds a LOT like the Order of the Sheltering Spire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=234819#post234819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. I'll maybe put a Compact together later that kind of reflects stuff on that, but otherwise, everything that needed to be said there has been.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a Compact is the wrong way to go about it. A Compact is an <i>answer</i>. But between Long Night, MM, Athenic Church, Sheltering Spire and Null Mysteriis, there are a lot of answers. What Cults need's is more about the questions. Fiction about hunters having a crisis of faith, or discussion in chapter five.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T15:50:48-07:00","id":235810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=235608#post235608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm honest, that sounds a LOT like the Order of the Sheltering Spire.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, true. I thought, at first, it was a little more different, more from being a paramilitary style organization, however,<br /> <br /> A. My description of them doesn't really have that come across,<br /> <br /> B. They still have a bit of similarity with preying on the vulnerable for recruits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think a Compact is the wrong way to go about it. A Compact is an <i>answer</i>. But between Long Night, MM, Athenic Church, Sheltering Spire and Null Mysteriis, there are a lot of answers. What Cults need's is more about the questions. Fiction about hunters having a crisis of faith, or discussion in chapter five. </div> </div> </div>True. Part of it would be, in this case, that perhaps the Compact forms to hunt Cults, well some at least, out of answers to those questions, especially as I don't quite think we have a Compact that that specifically hunts Cults yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","user":"Killer300","date":". 08-20-2014, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T00:32:30-07:00","id":236263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=235810#post235810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, true. I thought, at first, it was a little more different, more from being a paramilitary style organization, however</div> </div> </div> </div> It's still the same core theme - a cult that preys upon people by promising safety from the monsters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=235810#post235810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. Part of it would be, in this case, that perhaps the Compact forms to hunt Cults, well some at least, out of answers to those questions, especially as I don't quite think we have a Compact that that specifically hunts Cults yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Between the core 12 and Habibti Ma (from Mortal Remains) - I think we're good for Compacts that hunt cults.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T08:12:44-07:00","id":236510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=236263#post236263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's still the same core theme - a cult that preys upon people by promising safety from the monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Between the core 12 and Habibti Ma (from Mortal Remains) - I think we're good for Compacts that hunt cults. </div> </div> </div>Good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T19:41:57-07:00","id":237629,"title":"","content":"Ok, about my cult;<br /> <br /> I was thinking they have a great deal of sympathy for Pretas, hungry ghosts. More than that, I think the idea is that the World of Darkness actually isn't the human world, but the world of the pretas, might be a good plan. Everything's so miserable, everything's so defined by wanting the intangible, that certain people who admit the supernatural exists might go on to say that since the world is obviously not the mundane and relatively stable human world, it must be something else. The cult are people who have begun to remember they are actually pretas and not human, as evinced by &quot;remembering&quot; their supernatural natures and abilities.<br /> <br /> Of course, this also leads into their nihilism and Gnostic aspects; since reincarnation as a preta means you weren't a very good person in your past life or finished a term in Naraka. Either way, any suffering you undergo is simply your abysmal Karma enforcing itself, including what the cult brings.<br /> <br /> In place of the slarecians, they serve (what they think of as) Vajrapani, the bodhisattva symbolizing raw power, and his two incarnations, the Nio. As pretas, they do not deserve the mercy of Buddha, but they will follow the &quot;tough love&quot; approach of the Nio, as they both purify themselves through maddening and painful meditation, and the world through their schemes to create chaos and enforce Karma, possibly shaking the rest of &quot;humanity&quot; out of the delusion they are actually humans.<br /> <br /> Good?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T05:31:09-07:00","id":238104,"title":"","content":"What makes you feel they should believe they are all Pretas? I ask because this design rules out one of their most potent recruiting tools - which is claiming that their Endowment is evidence of Enlgihtenment and recruiting people with their ability to teach the Endowment.<br /> <br /> As for Vajrapani. I definately like your original idea of disembodied god-tier psychic minds. There's no reason they can't associate those minds with any particular bodhisattva; I'll have to read more about Vajrapani though. While Vajrapani may or may not exist in the world of darkness. And while WoD!Vajrapani may or may not resemble the one real world Buddhists talk about. The cult will definately know their scripture and only call something Vajrapani if it looks like the scriptures.<br /> <br /> I actually have a draft in my head - what can I say, it's an awesome concept that inspired me. I might have something you can look at in a day or so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-23-2014, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T06:51:24-07:00","id":238153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=238104#post238104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes you feel they should believe they are all Pretas? I ask because this design rules out one of their most potent recruiting tools - which is claiming that their Endowment is evidence of Enlgihtenment and recruiting people with their ability to teach the Endowment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually playing Digital Devil Saga, and had a fit of inspiration.<br /> <br /> Basically, the first game, as gradually shown, is actually a training simulator for Combat AI programs...who are actually reincarnations (in the Hindu sense) of people who were killed during the real world's apocalypse (how the apocalypse happened, according to the resistance there, is something I take umbridge with, but it's implied they're wrong in universe). Thing is, you see from the perspective of the AIs as they (re)gain the ability to feel emotions and gradually realize how strange their world is, and that they remember things they didn't do (as AIs). Up until the sequel, they don't quite grok they aren't normal humans, even as they gradually realize how incomplete their world is (for example, they only realize that &quot;children&quot; are a thing that exists about halfway through).<br /> <br /> That same sense of there being something very very wrong with the universe as how bizarre the whole thing is impresses itself on everyone was what tickled my brain. Yes, the cult is probably wrong, but the idea that the supernatural being a sign of something very important being very non-present stuck with me. Not to mention that what happened to begin the reclamation of memory and awakening to the artificial nature of the world seems pertinent to the nWoD in general; everyone in the simulation was infected by a virus that turned them all into shapeshifters.<br /> <br /> And of course, this also serves as a convenient explanation for all the human-derived supernaturals (&quot;Ah, well they were touched by something that reminds them of a specific way they are not actually human, and so have remembered a way to use their power to affect this illusion we call the real world, and themselves...but are simultaneously bound tighter by it, because they don't realize that their delusions just have more elements of truth&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T09:26:22-07:00","id":238272,"title":"","content":"Interesting, to say the least, but how would ghosts themselves work in this worldview? From what I know of Bhuddism, it doesn't really have a place for something like undead spirits, unless I'm missing something out of gross ignorance. Now, you did say this is really more Gnosticism, so there's that. Otherwise, perhaps they'd view it as someone trapped between the cycles of reincarnation? Being trapped would explain more limited behavior. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T10:15:22-07:00","id":238306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=238272#post238272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting, to say the least, but how would ghosts themselves work in this worldview? From what I know of Bhuddism, it doesn't really have a place for something like undead spirits, unless I'm missing something out of gross ignorance. Now, you did say this is really more Gnosticism, so there's that. Otherwise, perhaps they'd view it as someone trapped between the cycles of reincarnation? Being trapped would explain more limited behavior.</div> </div> </div> </div>First of course, they're a cult formed around the wonderful weirdness that is the WoD Cosmology, and acknowledging it doesn't look much like the human world as described in Buddhism or Hinduism (and I will be the first to admit I don't know precisely where one religion's cosmology begins and another begins). Heterodoxy is expected and encouraged, especially given how these guys blatantly ignore all the bits about compassion except when it's convenient.<br /> <br /> Second, there actually is a place for tradtional ghosts in Indian folk belief I'm pretty sure they can pick up; <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bhoot_(ghost)\" target=\"_blank\">Bhoots</a>. Even if we're drawing more from Tibet, there are ghosts there too. Admittedly, that's a preta, and it doesn't make sense in the context of their belief system, but...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 08-23-2014, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T14:39:57-07:00","id":238540,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Biv2X4DlUnTHxY0E9Czrikea6BOSs1gYkcsJ-i1aAnQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here's what I have so far.</a> Now to find someone who can say if this feels Buddhist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=238153#post238153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually playing Digital Devil Saga, and had a fit of inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me of the Red X guard from the webcomic Magellan (well worth reading)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-23-2014, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T16:21:41-07:00","id":238658,"title":"","content":"Hey, I started writing up a Compact last night in a fit of inspiration, and it's looking like it might work better as a Tier One or Two cult instead...kind of in a grey area. No religious themes though, at least not as I see it thus far. Are you looking specifically for faith-based groups or using &quot;Cult&quot; as a catchall?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2709-quatrevingts","name":"QuatreVingts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T20:01:04-07:00","id":238817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=238540#post238540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Biv2X4DlUnTHxY0E9Czrikea6BOSs1gYkcsJ-i1aAnQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here's what I have so far.</a> Now to find someone who can say if this feels Buddhist.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my own dime-store understanding, I think these guys could use a little more ideology, invoking a bit of Hinduism into the thing.<br /> <br /> Basically, one of the things often forgotten about the Kali Yuga (the Last Age of the World before Vishnu goes to bed, the one we're in right now) is that it's a great time to seek enlightenment; the world's suffering has become so great, so inescapable, that letting go of it becomes relatively easy. It's not as painful to let go of things that hurt you, after all, and doing good is something that in these dark times where it is a truly thankless task means it is done purely for the sake of having done good, uncorrupted by expectation of reward.<br /> <br /> I expect the reason they manipulate things into becoming increasingly shitty all around is a version of that; if suffering brings enlightenment and growth, than ensuring the world suffers is actually a sublime act of charity. That, and a lot of them don't feel like doing the world any favors, and it helps them gain power and influence. A desire fulfilled is a desire that no longer troubles them, after all, and they can also help mold the world into an environment favorable to their faith.<br /> <br /> (Naturally that last part is going to start raising alarm bells with mainstream Buddhists).<br /> <br /> There's been some scares about fundamentalist Buddhists, recently, too; might be worth looking into the 969 Movement, the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ikk%C5%8D-sh%C5%AB\" target=\"_blank\">Ikko-shu</a> and similar things for inspiration. Naturally the Empty Monastery feels much less bound to the idea of nationalism, but I can imagine them helping other religions destroy themselves and running secular power into the ground. To them, a state is simply another attachment in need of being severed or taught its own mortality. Especially if they feel rather bitter about something the state/corporation in recent years did; I can see them arising in the wake of the Rape of Nanking or the conquest of Tibet. And ironically, they don't let go of these things (if the former, I can easily see a plot hook where it's hinted they provoked the Lost Generation of Japan as long-overdue, pointless retribution).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T00:18:09-07:00","id":238917,"title":"","content":"Creating suffering to inspire people to escape suffering seems like a good idea.<br /> <br /> Actually; I've been haveing trouble thinking of a quote for them. I might have one now.<br /> <br /> You're suffering has brought you far<br /> Now let go<br /> And see the world with new eyes.<br /> <br /> Though I might go on a binge of famous Buddhist sayings and try to Frankenstein something similar out of quotes to make it sound more authentic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QuatreVingts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=238658#post238658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I started writing up a Compact last night in a fit of inspiration, and it's looking like it might work better as a Tier One or Two cult instead...kind of in a grey area. No religious themes though, at least not as I see it thus far. Are you looking specifically for faith-based groups or using &quot;Cult&quot; as a catchall?</div> </div> </div> </div>Catchall, providing they brainwash their own members in some form they're golden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-24-2014, 04:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T17:18:27-07:00","id":245070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/188087-hunter-cults-development-revival-thread?p=238917#post238917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creating suffering to inspire people to escape suffering seems like a good idea.<br /> <br /> Catchall, providing they brainwash their own members in some form they're golden.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, with just a little tweaking they'll be <i>perfect </i>for that, then: They're hippies. &gt;:]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2709-quatrevingts","name":"Qua